<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25908" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δια-στᾰτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
		also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Lyd.
			<u>Mens.</u>
			4.76
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>torn by
				faction,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					515
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>having extension</i> or <i>dimension,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶμα δ. τριχῇ</span> Apollodor.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				3.259
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.8
			</span></i>, etc.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμερής,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				176
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πάντῃ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1023b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. πράγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					375
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τῶς</span>
			<i>dimensionally</i> or <i>in extension,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Sent.</u>
				33
			</span></i>, Syrian, <i><span class="en">
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				85.14
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοερῶς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>in Cra.</u>
				p.55
			</span></i> P.</div>
